  "scope": "One disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster runs a namespace-scoped Python control loop against a case-owned numeric telemetry ConfigMap. The loop reads an explicit enabled flag and threshold, records a deterministic decision ConfigMap, and when enabled and value >= threshold patches only the target Deployment scale subresource to zero. The halt stays latched across restart. The test observes Deployment status and EndpointSlices and retains a separate available control Deployment. It proves this synthetic controller/API/RBAC path only; it does not establish production telemetry authenticity, policy governance, workload coverage, response-time objectives, serving-layer isolation, or training/pipeline Job behavior.",
